method.description:
Returns an [Array] of dictionaries with copyright information for every component of OpenVic's source code.
Every [Dictionary] contains a [code]name[/code] identifier, and a [code]parts[/code] array of dictionaries. It describes the component in detail with the following entries:
- [code]files[/code] - [Array] of file paths from the source code affected by this component;
- [code]copyright[/code] - [Array] of owners of this component;
- [code]license[/code] - The license applied to this component (such as "[url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIT_License#Ambiguity_and_variants]MIT[/url]" or "[url=https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/]CC-BY-4.0[/url]").

Returns the current game version information as a [Dictionary] containing the following entries:
- [code]tag[/code] - Full release tag as a String, "<tag missing>" if OpenVic has no tag;
- [code]major[/code] - Major version number as an int, 0 if OpenVic has no tag;
- [code]minor[/code] - Minor version number as an int, 2 if OpenVic has no tag;
- [code]patch[/code] - Patch version number as an int, 0 if OpenVic has no tag;
- [code]prerelease_type[/code] - Pre-release type (such as "nightly", "snapshot", "snapshot.dev", "alpha", "beta", or "rc"), "" if regular release, "unknown" if OpenVic has no tag;
- [code]prerelease_count[/code] - Pre-release number as an int, 0 if regular release or if OpenVic has no tag;
- [code]prerelease_hash[/code] - Pre-release tag hash as a String, "" if regular release, "unknown" if OpenVic has no tag;
- [code]hex[/code] - Full version encoded as a hexadecimal int with one byte (2 hex digits) per number (see example below);
- [code]release[/code] - Human-readable Release name as a String, same as [code]tag[/code] if release name unknown;
- [code]hash[/code] - Full Git commit hash as a String;
- [code]timestamp[/code] - Holds the Git commit date UNIX timestamp in seconds as an int, or [code]0[/code] if unavailable;
The [code]hex[/code] value is encoded as follows, from left to right: one byte for the major, one byte for the minor, one byte for the patch version. For example, "3.1.12" would be [code]0x03010C[/code].
[b]Note:[/b] The [code]hex[/code] value is still an [int] internally, and printing it will give you its decimal representation, which is not particularly meaningful. Use hexadecimal literals for quick version comparisons from code:
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
if OVGame.get_version_info().hex >= 0x040100:
	pass # Do things specific to version 4.1 or later.
else:
	pass # Do things specific to versions before 4.1.
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
if ((int)OVGame.GetVersionInfo()["hex"] >= 0x040100)
{
	// Do things specific to version 4.1 or later.
}
else
{
	// Do things specific to versions before 4.1.
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
